; ============================================================================
; GROUP NATIVE FAILURE -- STAGE (AIF-160)
;
; The same two members as GRPFAIL, dirtied through NATIVE table buffers rather
; than SQLSEL, and left dirty across the script boundary. DOTSCRIPT runs in
; this process, so the areas, the buffers and the open journals all survive
; into the commit script.
;
; WHY A SECOND FIXTURE EXISTS AT ALL, and it is not duplication. GRPFAIL drives
; SQLSEL, whose release_sql_transaction walks every member into
; journal_note_rollback -- which refuses to delete a decided journal AND CLOSES
; ITS HANDLE. After that COMMIT cannot write anything, because
; journal_begin_commit returns early on a null FILE*. GROUPCOMMIT has NO
; teardown: it gathers members, commits, prints, and walks away from an OPEN
; handle over a durable P. That open handle is the entire subject of this arm.
;
; TABLE BUFFER ON PERSISTENT is the only spelling that reaches persistence from
; the command surface -- the `on` handler takes persistent/journal/ram tokens,
; applies the mode, enables the buffer, and calls journal_note_buffer_on. There
; is no SET TABLE BUFFER PERSISTENT; cmd_set.cpp knows only ON|OFF [ALL].
;
; NO SQL MODE HERE. GROUPCOMMIT refuses outright while a SQL transaction is
; active, and says so.
; ============================================================================

SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES/SANDBOX
SET PATH LMDB LMDB/SANDBOX

FORMULA "GRPNATIVE-STAGE-BEGIN"

SELECT 1
USE GRPFAIL1
TABLE BUFFER ON PERSISTENT

SELECT 2
USE GRPFAIL2
TABLE BUFFER ON PERSISTENT

; THE PERSISTENCE GUARDS, and they are here because the alternative is an arm
; that passes for a fourth wrong reason. Under RamOnly there is no journal, no
; P record and no handle, so every assertion downstream would be satisfied by
; a transaction that never wrote a log at all. journal_note_buffer_on opens the
; .tbj at buffer-on, so the files must exist RIGHT NOW, before anything is
; staged. If either reads .F. the rest of this arm is measuring nothing.
? "GN_P1_member_one_journal_armed:" + FILE("DBF/SANDBOX/GRPFAIL1.dbf.tbj")
? "GN_P2_member_two_journal_armed:" + FILE("DBF/SANDBOX/GRPFAIL2.dbf.tbj")

; Both buffers dirty, neither committed. USE lands on record 1 of a one-record
; table, so no navigation is needed and none is spelled.
SELECT 1
REPLACE MARK WITH "AFTER"
SELECT 2
REPLACE MARK WITH "AFTER"
SELECT 1

FORMULA "GRPNATIVE-STAGE-END"
